  Using a lot more boulders to fill up space helps.  The fewer squares
where monsters can randomly generate (or be summoned) the better.
Elbereth under everything.  At some point you'll probably want to
b?oGeno giants, to stop them being generated on top of your boulders.
(Be sure you have all the boulders you want from randomly generated
giants first.)


  Be prepared to tame some archons.  They can patrol nearby areas.  That
will keep you from being disturbed by "You feel monsters are aware of
your presence," etc.


  Other problems are randomly generated monsters breaking your boulders,
killing mimics, and destroying holy water and scrolls of remove curse
that are on the ground.  Dragons are a big offender here.  b?oGenocide
can help.  (The !oHW and b?oRC are in case your polearm gets cursed and
welded to your hands.)





